{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/621642-help-me-make-houston-even-worse","id":621642,"title":"Help me make Houston even worse","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-09T15:07:58-07:00","id":621642,"title":"Help me make Houston even worse","content":"Hello all, I have a game set in Texas during the 1840s, and I have wanted to present Houston and most of Harris county as a stronghold of the Wyrm. Cities are traditionally painted as being places rife with spiritual corruption, but I want to make Houston special. Historically the sometimes-capitol always had a rough, dangerous reputation, and lechery, widespread drunkenness and unthinking violence were common. I want there to be something really nasty holed up there, something insidious that can't just be torn to ribbons by a bunch of marauding Garou. I want there to be something (other than a Black Spiral Dancer pit) that could force a Garou sept into something akin to a stalemate or a cold war. I am not sure how I want to go about that, however, and I am looking to pick your brains for suggestions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T02:01:12-07:00","id":621974,"title":"","content":"The City Father. Yeah, theoretically Houston shouldn't have one until much later (well into the 20th century when the whole place is huge), but some hints have been dropped that City Fathers can actually exist outside the bounds of time to a degree. Given that Endron (in the World of Darkness) and Enron (in the real world) were both headquartered there, that has some rather nasty implications for what the City Father of Houston would be like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T06:04:41-07:00","id":622093,"title":"","content":"If you have the Apocalypse book there is a nasty little race in the book that could easily take the place of BSD. One form of Wyrm creatures from the 1st edition that never made the jump to others the Gamor could easily become the true mastermind. The Gamor at least as originally written could become a kind of psychic vampire that manipulates emotions creating turmoil and violence to feed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T19:59:50-07:00","id":623047,"title":"","content":"I'd take advantage that Houston is in oil country by placing some horrible ancient evil underneath there in the oil. Even though the 1840s is before the advent of the petroleum industry, the evil could still be active - corrupting local Indians of long ago into evil cultists, using the Spanish or Texans into wiping out the good indian kinfolk of the Garou keeping it in check, and manipulating a cult in the city to grow and develop it as a concrete and metal fortress to protect it against the Garou.<br /> <br /> What the evil is up to you. It could just be a Bane trapped there by the Uktena or a Cthulhu like alien or a remnant of Earth before the current form of the biosphere was formed. It could have its origins in the petroleum itself, or it could simply be using the petroleum as a medium to exist in, or just occupying the same place.<br /> <br /> Whatever it is though; it is hostile to Gaia and wants to belch forth the rancid fumes of industry and commerce to change the biosphere into something better for itself... or its &quot;people&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T22:15:37-07:00","id":623129,"title":"","content":"Hey guys, thanks for the replies. Seems like we argue endlessly over rules but brainstorming seems to generate less exited responses- but that is not the case here. These are all good ideas. I will likely go with a combination of the oil bane/City Father concept. Something predatory should be spurring the burgeoning city's growth, and I like the idea of a cthonic entity devouring all around it through industry.<br /> <br /> In terms of fortresses, I have already introduced a creeping corruption that involves naturae spirits dying, and rather than dissipatin once their essence is exhausted, they wither and die, their un-rotting husks littering the penumbra (sort of like a spiritual version of Qlippothic matter). Get enough dead gafflings and jagglings together and you might be able to scrape them into a pretty bizarre and terrible fortification.<br /> <br /> I just used the idea of another race of creatures (unpleasant aquatic beasts called Igohida, Cherokee for 'Eternal'), so perhaps Gamor being in east Texas also might be a bit similar; that said, there are characteristics of the Gamor that I really like. Most of the bad things I have been using for this chapter have been servants of the Defiler Wyrm, so something that manipulates and twists emotions to darker desires or self-destruction could fit right in...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}